maps are embedded in nodes

LNodes for logical Nodes
SNodes for simple-merged nodes, indeed a LNode with a partial key
FNodes for fdm nodes, indeed a single ART node (which could point to other type nodes)
CNodes for cdn nodes, default for 4 diff positions, and related strings


## Why We Need Micro-Leaf (CLeaf, FLeaf)

In short, to represent the dot.
Speculating the dot by the length of processed bytes is not sufficient.
Consider following keys:
"abcd.r1, abcdef.r2, abcdfg.r3"
And now we are processing "abcd.r1" and that "abcd" has been processed.
Coincidentally, there three keys are routed by same pointer, i.e.,
in the node we are at now, we should do an "empty jump" to avoid verifying on "ef.r2" or "fg.r3".
However, by calculating the processed bytes length, the next path "r1" has been passed in and
it is impossible to differ whether we should do the empty jump.

两种方案，
1. 无论当前状态如何，都要尝试 empty jump，没有空间开销，但需要更多时间
2. 设置一种 micro leaf 来代表分隔符，时间上简单了，但增加了很多空间
方案 2 最终会被避免：当我们将 path 看作完整的字符串而不是分段字符串，其实 2 就被回避了。